<comment datatype='string'>&lt;a href=&quot;/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=MONOMER-11936&quot;&gt;(&lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;)-3-hydroxybutyryl-CoA dehydrogenase&lt;/a&gt; (BHBD) is one of the enzymes in the central fermentation pathway of &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-1520&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Clostridium beijerinckii&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. It catalyzes the first committed step in the production of &lt;a href=&quot;/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=BUTYRIC_ACID&quot;&gt;butanoate&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=BUTANOL&quot;&gt;butan-1-ol&lt;/a&gt;.
&lt;p&gt;
BHBD enzymes can be specific for either the (&lt;i&gt;R&lt;/i&gt;) or (&lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;) isomers of 3-hydroxybutyryl-CoA, and can be either NADH- or NADPH-dependent [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/19304817&quot;&gt;Tseng09&lt;/a&gt;]. The &lt;a href=&quot;/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=G-97&quot;&gt;hbd&lt;/a&gt;-encoded enzyme from &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-1520&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Clostridium beijerinckii&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is (&lt;i&gt;S&lt;/i&gt;)-specific, and has higher processivity using NADH [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/1444364&quot;&gt;Colby92&lt;/a&gt;].
&lt;p&gt;
An NADPH-dependent &lt;a href=&quot;/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=MONOMER-13586&quot;&gt;(&lt;i&gt;R&lt;/i&gt;)-3-hydroxybutyryl-CoA dehydrogenase&lt;/a&gt; has been characterized from &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-1063&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Cereibacter sphaeroides&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. That enzyme is encoded by the &lt;a href=&quot;/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=G-10357&quot;&gt;phaB&lt;/a&gt; gene [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/16856937&quot;&gt;Alber06&lt;/a&gt;]. The bacterium &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-381666&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Cupriavidus necator&lt;/i&gt; H16&lt;/a&gt; appears to possess both enzymes [&lt;a href=&quot;/META/reference.html?type=CITATION-REFERENCE&amp;object=%5bHaywood88%5d&quot;&gt;Haywood88&lt;/a&gt;].</comment>
